# Licence of the captured data

**This is not an open-data repository in the sense the rest of this fleet is.**
Most sources it holds are Open Government Licence or US federal works. This one
is not, and the difference is load-bearing.

## The source

WHO applies **CC BY-NC-SA 3.0 IGO** to its content and specifies no separate
licence for its website, so that is what the captured pages carry:

- <https://www.who.int/about/policies/publishing/copyright>
- <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/3.0/igo/>

What it means, in the three parts that matter here:

| | |
| --- | --- |
| **BY** | attribution to WHO is required |
| **NC** | **non-commercial use only** — commercial reuse needs WHO's written permission, via WHO's permissions form |
| **SA** | derivatives must be shared under the same licence |

WHO further states that its materials may not be used to promote a product or
an organisation, that the WHO logo needs separate written authorisation, and
that WHO gives no warranty of any kind.

## What that means for this archive

The raw captures under `raw/` and the tables under `derived/` are reproductions
and derivatives of WHO material, and they inherit the licence above. They are
published here for **non-commercial** research and public-interest use, with
attribution to WHO as the source of the underlying list.

**If you intend any commercial use, your permission has to come from WHO, not
from this repository.** Nothing here can grant it.

## What this repository's own work is licensed as

The code — the engine configuration in `registry/`, the parsers in `parsers/`,
the workflows — is MIT, as in `LICENSE`. That covers the software only, and
does not and cannot relicense WHO's data.

